  "query_preview": "/SUNDAY THROUGH WEDNESDAY/...\nIssued at 238 AM CST Thu Nov 12 2026\n\nOn Sunday, cyclonic flow will give way to upper-level shortwave \nridging or a general weakness in flow as longwave troughing across \nthe Great Lakes and Northeast finally progresses eastward. In this \nprocess, the surface anticyclone will be slow to retreat \nnortheastward early next week with only a very gradual moderation of \ntemperatures toward average, mainly from airmass modification versus \nadvection at least through Tuesday. Global model guidance is in \nreasonable agreement that the anticyclone will retreat enough for \nlow-level southerly WAA to increase after Tuesday with temperatures \nwarming above average. Otherwise, confidence has further increased \nin CWA-wide dry conditions prevailing through this period with \nglobal ensemble model probabilities of measurable rainfall now below \n10 percent with the weakening upper-level trough trending further \nsouth of the CWA Sunday into Monday.",
